                <head>280. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>After attending the third emergency special session of the U.N. General Assembly,
                    Foreign Minister Couve de Murville traveled to Washington August 21 for talks
                    with Acting Secretary Herter and President Eisenhower. That afternoon,
                    Eisenhower raised the subject of Algeria. A memorandum of this conversation is
                    scheduled for publication in <ref target="frus:frus1958-60v07p1">volume
                        VII</ref>.</p>
            </div>
